      "documentConcept": "PD staging: Hoehn-Yahr, Braak and biological SynNeurGe",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:dc577dff35151487f8ab606dd21cc764d55477724ac6ec273660531ee35c88d6",
      "text": "Hoehn–Yahr describes motor disability, especially laterality, balance and physical independence. Braak staging describes a proposed sequence of postmortem α-synuclein pathology; exceptions limit its interpretation as a universal course or clinical severity measure. SynNeurGe combines synuclein pathology, neurodegeneration and genetics with clinical manifestations for research classification. Its authors explicitly refrained from proposing a temporal staging sequence, distinguishing it from NSD-ISS. These frameworks answer different questions and should be identified by name when comparing research populations. The NSD-ISS has been applied to PPMI, PASADENA and SPARK data.",
